}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:50:41-07:00","id":713192,"title":"","content":"Well, given this is a Werewolf book, I suspect you'll be disappointed in the lack of explicit mentions about other supernaturals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When a Garou is ripping out the heart of Khara she probably isn't thinking about ghosts or fairies or wizards or vampires. Got other things on her mind, and all that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:58:09-07:00","id":713336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=713192#post713192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, given this is a Werewolf book, I suspect you'll be disappointed in the lack of explicit mentions about other supernaturals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When a Garou is ripping out the heart of Khara she probably isn't thinking about ghosts or fairies or wizards or vampires. Got other things on her mind, and all that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Right but when the cealican(sp) start running and hiding in Fairyland it might come up?<br /> <br /> or if say Mezoamerica was filled with vampires playing at being gods in the cities it might make the Garou look less dumb in their reaction to the Bats<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T19:27:43-07:00","id":713489,"title":"","content":"It might come up, but only as a side mention to the actual events though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:28:44-07:00","id":714831,"title":"","content":"Enough cryptic clues. The Kickstarter is live, go learn the answers! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:50:30-07:00","id":714910,"title":"","content":"So I see that you went with Blood and Silk making Chiyou a Garou in spite of all of his associations with bulls. And he's confined to hell for fighting the Wan Xian. Not really happy about including that, or enthusiastic about the time travel adventure. This doesn't seem to be my cup of tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T21:13:59-07:00","id":717188,"title":"","content":"Can you potentially spoil some of the stuff from the last chapter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T21:28:19-07:00","id":717218,"title":"","content":"Probably not since it's only being redlined now, so everything is up for changing. I can say I'm in love with the War of Dragons though. And the War of Tears was quite sad to research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T22:54:30-07:00","id":717457,"title":"","content":"Can you tell us abit about the War of the Dragons that seems to be a new thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T23:24:43-07:00","id":717535,"title":"","content":"The chronicle is pretty good beat to beat, but I find myself feeling a bit put off by the push to correct these time streams and any deviation potentially leading to Apocalypse. A huge part of WtA is that wrong actions and bad choices led to the current almost no-win scenario the garou struggle with in the present day. To replicate these actions because they were the 'correct' ones, it makes the whole thing seem inevitable. Which makes the garou's guilt lesser.<br /> <br /> And, yes, I know the reason you have to fix them is due Wyrmish influence. But having characters go to these events and seeing their complexity first hand. And still correcting them to how history -should- have gone, what does it actually tell the characters? That they shouldn't feel guilty of the past, because it could have been worse? Heck, what about the poor Fera?<br /> <br /> Looking at Past Lives, it has a similar idea. But it never directly gives the PCs ability to truly affect the events, they are too big to ever for one pack to try and heal. Yet, they still -can- affect things so a single White Howler ancestor can be their contact in the future.<br /> <br /> Here, you might have a real chance heal them. I think it would be better if instead of fera and garou unity in the bad future, some tribes or fera would be just -lost-. That way, correcting the streams would have a sense of 'well, the alternative was so bad even this is better'. And fighting would still break out if certain tribes/fera would be -worth- saving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T23:37:08-07:00","id":717614,"title":"","content":"Any chance that the aforementioned cut Caine and Abel stuff can be posted? I'm not sure what the rules are on cut material, but I'm a big fan of crossover stuff, and really ancient days. Love the idea of Shattered Dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 10-23-2015, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T23:54:27-07:00","id":717684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=717457#post717457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you tell us abit about the War of the Dragons that seems to be a new thing</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet. First drafts are in, redlines are happening. <br /> <br /> Soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T02:44:47-07:00","id":718359,"title":"","content":"I want to state, I hope we see rules for resources for pre history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T05:57:20-07:00","id":718716,"title":"","content":"Yeah, me too! I did write a condensed - like, no seriously condensed - over view of available technological advances for my first draft. Just wasn't room for them in the end. And, I mean, they were barely English. :/ <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also started one for Rites and Gifts but there's no way that would have ever fit without tons of explanation, so I dropped the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:20:41-07:00","id":720127,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm sneaking back in for another KS. This should be fun! Glad to see it's off to a good start already, and looking forward to see the final results. Big thanks to OP, and everyone who's worked on this, and all the other books. It's nice to see the WoD back and running strong once more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We'll ride the Spiral to the end, we may just go where no one's been...<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3188-vermiis","name":"Vermiis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T14:59:31-07:00","id":729980,"title":"","content":"This is the book I never knew I wanted, but now that I know it exists, I want it. I'm sure it'll have it's own special character sheet for the pre-historic setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T03:55:15-07:00","id":737548,"title":"","content":"Vould you comment on my posts in this thread?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi\"> Shattered Dreams: some inconsistencies regarding the Ananasi - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The unedited draft states at multiple times that the Ananasi are spreading the Weaver's influence. Chapter 2 furthermore states that they are doing so because their Queen is inside her opal prison and so they must obey. In W20 Changing Breed 20, though, the authors went with the old version from the </div> </div> </div><br /> in synthesis:<br /> The Aanasi are presented multiple times as serving the Weaver while in fact they served the Wyrm while Ananasa was held hostage and they never took orders from the Weaver in their history (I kinda eel like this is a gross inconsistency that can't be handwaved with &quot;yeah well they don't know their history&quot;)<br /> <br /> The Camazotz are referred, multiple times, as being vulnerable to gold, again in contraddiction to W20 Changing Breeds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T04:15:40-07:00","id":737626,"title":"","content":"I'd reckon the best way to think about it, is that the Ananasi aren't a singular monolithic entity. Lots of Ananasi exist over the years, and some of them do the Weaver's bidding, and some of them do the Wyld's and some of them do the Wyrm's. Some of them serve no one, others serve all of them over time.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately when wordcount is so limited writing that every time gets prohibitive, so generalities get used, which will never be as specific as you'd (the general you, not you you) would like.<br /> <br /> Also, the time spans involved definitely muddy events. Not to mention trying to pinpoint a date such as 'Queen Ananasa is taken hostage by the Wyrm'. That way lies madness! (Though I have my own thoughts on the matter, those are purely fan ideas).<br /> <br /> As for the Camazotz and gold thing. Maybe 7000 years ago it was true. At some point they managed to flip the bane from gold to silver! That'd be interesting... lots of epic questing involved. Or maybe there was a line of werebats that were allergic to gold, and then they all died out (possibly cuz of garou wielding gold against them).<br /> Food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":167,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","user":"nikink","date":".  ideas! 10-29-2015, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T08:35:54-07:00","id":738410,"title":"","content":"Could it be that sometimes when the Khan are mentioned in the raw text that it was autocorrected from Khara? Or were the weretigers native to Africa at some point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:15:38-07:00","id":739426,"title":"","content":"Too long ago to recall exactly, but I suspect it's the latter. Plus outliers from individuals being able to travel as they wish, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T05:45:17-07:00","id":741445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=737548#post737548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vould you comment on my posts in this thread?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi\"> Shattered Dreams: some inconsistencies regarding the Ananasi - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The unedited draft states at multiple times that the Ananasi are spreading the Weaver's influence. Chapter 2 furthermore states that they are doing so because their Queen is inside her opal prison and so they must obey. In W20 Changing Breed 20, though, the authors went with the old version from the </div> </div> </div><br /> in synthesis:<br /> The Aanasi are presented multiple times as serving the Weaver while in fact they served the Wyrm while Ananasa was held hostage and they never took orders from the Weaver in their history (I kinda eel like this is a gross inconsistency that can't be handwaved with &quot;yeah well they don't know their history&quot;)<br /> <br /> The Camazotz are referred, multiple times, as being vulnerable to gold, again in contraddiction to W20 Changing Breeds</div> </div> </div> </div>For anyone wondering, I've responded to these comments in the original thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:31:15-07:00","id":742686,"title":"","content":"Question on &quot;Time Streams&quot;:<br /> <br /> First of all, I like the idea -- playing on Quantum Theory and all is cool. The thing that comes to mind is, will there be any explanation of how this differs from, say, Mirror Zones? Up to now, it's been very difficult to muck with time even with the biggest, baddest magic -- but not <i>impossible</i>. The hang-up has always been that if you goof with time too radically from what it's supposed to be, the path of least resistance is that you essentially get trapped in a Mirror Zone that represents the changes that you &quot;made&quot; to the timeline -- ignorant that you're not in the &quot;real world&quot; anymore, and ignorant that the existing timeline is chugging merrily on without you.<br /> <br /> Or, more to the point: Will it be that Time Streams and Mirror Zones are, in fact, the <i>same thing</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:36:24-07:00","id":742919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=742686#post742686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on &quot;Time Streams&quot;:<br /> <br /> First of all, I like the idea -- playing on Quantum Theory and all is cool. The thing that comes to mind is, will there be any explanation of how this differs from, say, Mirror Zones? Up to now, it's been very difficult to muck with time even with the biggest, baddest magic -- but not <i>impossible</i>. The hang-up has always been that if you goof with time too radically from what it's supposed to be, the path of least resistance is that you essentially get trapped in a Mirror Zone that represents the changes that you &quot;made&quot; to the timeline -- ignorant that you're not in the &quot;real world&quot; anymore, and ignorant that the existing timeline is chugging merrily on without you.<br /> <br /> Or, more to the point: Will it be that Time Streams and Mirror Zones are, in fact, the <i>same thing</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mirror Zones? Never heard of that. Is it a Mage thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:31:47-07:00","id":743301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=742919#post742919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mirror Zones? Never heard of that. Is it a Mage thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was in the Umbra Revised, possibly the first one as well. They're weird false realities where things are not as they should be, which can range from something very subtle to blatant oddities, one being given in the book as &quot;Kenny G is president for life of the USA in a coup backed by Jesse Ventura&quot;.. Getting out of one involves coming to a resolution with the deviations from reality.<br /> <br /> (This entire setup makes me think of a game of W:tA run through the plot of Abenobashi Magical Shopping Arcade, incidentally.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:35:32-07:00","id":743663,"title":"","content":"They're basically alternate timelines that may or may not actually be equally real... they probably aren't, as I understand the book, but they might be, or PCs can start thinking they're real. Each one contains its own entire Umbra and planet Earth.<br /> <br /> I think another possibility mentioned was a world in which the Garou lost the Wars of Rage. Too lazy to go check my book. No timelines got actual descriptions, they're entirely for the ST to create.<br /> <br /> They also go along with Temporal Zones, which are like simulations of past eras, and maybe of possible futures. Visitors might think they're time-travelling, and may even emerge &quot;back in the present&quot; in a Mirror Zone in which they &quot;changed history.&quot;<br /> <br /> *cues creepy music*<br /> <br /> Of course, an ST can make the Mirrors and time travel as real and valid as they want.<br /> <br /> The adventure Past Lives also has a funky pseudo-time-travel story, although the point is for the PCs to experience the past and learn lessons from great tragedies, not to have an opportunity to change them. Aaaand I think that was the first book to give us written Gifts for Apis, Grondr, Camaztoz, and White Howlers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-30-2015, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T23:08:41-07:00","id":743891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=742686#post742686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on &quot;Time Streams&quot;:<br /> <br /> First of all, I like the idea -- playing on Quantum Theory and all is cool. The thing that comes to mind is, will there be any explanation of how this differs from, say, Mirror Zones? Up to now, it's been very difficult to muck with time even with the biggest, baddest magic -- but not <i>impossible</i>. The hang-up has always been that if you goof with time too radically from what it's supposed to be, the path of least resistance is that you essentially get trapped in a Mirror Zone that represents the changes that you &quot;made&quot; to the timeline -- ignorant that you're not in the &quot;real world&quot; anymore, and ignorant that the existing timeline is chugging merrily on without you.<br /> <br /> Or, more to the point: Will it be that Time Streams and Mirror Zones are, in fact, the <i>same thing</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To change history you need to gain control of a number of very powerful Caerns, until then history stays the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T01:58:12-07:00","id":743991,"title":"","content":"You're mixing up Feng Shui and Werewolf. Which amuses me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T03:45:24-07:00","id":744156,"title":"","content":"Haven't made it to the end of the uneditied document yet, (too busy with Exalted &amp; Beast) but I do hope that it provides a sidebar for those players who don't want to ditch some of their 'time-displaced' characters after Nightmaster afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T13:23:03-07:00","id":744937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=743991#post743991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're mixing up Feng Shui and Werewolf. Which amuses me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah I just think Feng Shui has one of the most playable methods of dealing with Time travel, and if I were to use this I'd straight up do it Ala Feng Shui.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T00:59:44-08:00","id":766913,"title":"","content":"Rich has added the War of Tears and War of Dragons first drafts to the Kickstarter doc, if anyone has been hanging out to see what we've cooked up for those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T12:17:51-08:00","id":767200,"title":"","content":"Regarding the exclusion of Squamus form in the Time of the Kings... the Mesozoic played host to many sharks of about that size, and the early Cretaceous was when familiar modern sharks started appearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T16:27:21-08:00","id":768162,"title":"","content":"I think the Time of Kings is interesting*, but I don't think it makes sense for the Mokole to be non-crocodiles. First of all, AFAIK plesiosaurs were all huge, so having one as an animal form means your Archid form is crazy giant... also they lose continuity with the Mokole if they don't have any crocodile or turtle forms. How did they survive for long enough to give them the time to change every one of them to breeding with new species of reptiles? I always thought the Mokole back then were crocodiles and sea crocodiles (and turtles and sea turtles, I guess) and their archid forms were dinosaurs and flying pterosaurs and (non-crocodile) sea reptiles and bird-dinos. My suggestion is to replace the plesiosaurs with crocodiles and sea-crocodiles, and ... I don't know. Maybe the origin of the Ao is tied to the change from Mnesis-as-a-place to Mnesis-as-a-curse? Or else just include the Ao... in other words the &quot;varni&quot; would be big categories instead of individual species: ao (turtle), suchid (crocodilian), pterosaur, and (relatively small) dinosaur.<br /> <br /> *I should be stoked and excited because this aspect of the Mokole is awesome. I honestly don't know why I'm so blah... maybe it's all this danged rain. Please pretend that I'm excited and jumping up and down. It's great that this is going in the book.<br /> <br /> <br /> One other thing... I hope the Drachid are portrayed as therapod dinosaurs with tails and horizontal posture, not human-shaped. Dinosaur skeletons make a human posture physically impossible, and I think reptoids look... silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Forgot to add: The names El-Kaataar, Alpeseak, and Tkash might be copywrite infringement. I don't know where El-Kaataar and Tkash came from, but Alpeasak (correct spelling IIRC), &quot;yilane&quot;, and most of the continent names in the Mokole Breedbook were taken from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_of_Eden\" target=\"_blank\">Eden trilogy</a> by Harry Harrison. Some other names and words (Sal-Afsan the Farseer, &quot;heesh&quot;, &quot;whileelin&quot;, &quot;quintaglio&quot;) in the Breedbook were taken from other Scifi books. I don't know if they were taken with permission in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-17-2015, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T17:28:29-08:00","id":768190,"title":"","content":"I agree with Erinys in regard to the animal breed forms. Adding the plesiosaurs and what not was very cool, but I think relying on their breeding rites to gain not just the homid form in place of Drachid but also new verna to replace extinct ones feels like too much of a deux ex machina. Besides as even the CB20 points out the Ao are old, very old....and well...<br /> <img src=\"https://40.media.tumblr.com/c29ac0954683c00738f954fc163f35d2/tumblr_mvheu00bY21spmwbxo1_400.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> TELL ME THIS WOULD NOT ROCK FOR AN ANIMAL FORM!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-17-2015, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T17:47:18-08:00","id":768199,"title":"","content":"For the record totally bringing in Gumagan Ao into my War of Tears run:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninjemys\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/Ninjemys_oweni.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninjemys\" target=\"_blank\"> Ninjemys - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninjemys\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninjemys </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T22:56:43-08:00","id":768294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768162#post768162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Time of Kings is interesting*, but I don't think it makes sense for the Mokole to be non-crocodiles. First of all, AFAIK plesiosaurs were all huge, so having one as an animal form means your Archid form is crazy giant... also they lose continuity with the Mokole if they don't have any crocodile or turtle forms. How did they survive for long enough to give them the time to change every one of them to breeding with new species of reptiles? I always thought the Mokole back then were crocodiles and sea crocodiles (and turtles and sea turtles, I guess) and their archid forms were dinosaurs and flying pterosaurs and (non-crocodile) sea reptiles and bird-dinos. My suggestion is to replace the plesiosaurs with crocodiles and sea-crocodiles, and ... I don't know. Maybe the origin of the Ao is tied to the change from Mnesis-as-a-place to Mnesis-as-a-curse? Or else just include the Ao... in other words the &quot;varni&quot; would be big categories instead of individual species: ao (turtle), suchid (crocodilian), pterosaur, and (relatively small) dinosaur.<br /> <br /> *I should be stoked and excited because this aspect of the Mokole is awesome. I honestly don't know why I'm so blah... maybe it's all this danged rain. Please pretend that I'm excited and jumping up and down. It's great that this is going in the book.<br /> <br /> <br /> One other thing... I hope the Drachid are portrayed as therapod dinosaurs with tails and horizontal posture, not human-shaped. Dinosaur skeletons make a human posture physically impossible, and I think reptoids look... silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, we already have a Reptoid form for modern Mokole. If Drachid is supposed to be lost, and yet exactly resembles the modern Mokole Near Human form, that would be odd, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T23:20:22-08:00","id":768303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768294#post768294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, we already have a Reptoid form for modern Mokole. If Drachid is supposed to be lost, and yet exactly resembles the modern Mokole Near Human form, that would be odd, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mokole don't have a near human form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T23:54:33-08:00","id":768319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768162#post768162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Time of Kings is interesting*, but I don't think it makes sense for the Mokole to be non-crocodiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, glad you find it interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Next, Dragon Kings aren't Mokole. Mokole came from the fallen Dragon Kings. Therefore, Mokole are crocodiles (and lizards etc.)<br /> <br /> Edit: This is possibly a little misleading. To be (hopefully) clearer, Mokole are the revised, fallen remnants of Dragon Kings. Dragon Kings are the Mokole in their full glory as they were originally meant to be. The two are the same, but different. <br /> <br /> Clearer? Probably not. Mokole are to Dragon Kings as Bunyip are to Garou. Still werewolves, but they've lost some things, and gained others. Edit ended. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thirdly, in my (biased) opinion, it makes more sense for Dragon Kings to be dinosaurs (and for this post, I'm using 'dinosaur' to include pterosaur and plesiosaur) than crocodilians and turtles. Dinosaurs existed from early in the Mesozoic and endured throughout. Turtles appeared about half way through the Mesozoic, and Crocs only appeared in the last 20 million years or so. By the time these animals appeared, Dragon Kings were well and truly established. They didn't need to be crocs etc. Also, what Dragon King would want to be a puny crocodilian? Being that small would be some kind of punishment, compared to their glorious dinosaur forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768162#post768162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, AFAIK plesiosaurs were all huge, so having one as an animal form means your Archid form is crazy giant</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they had crazy-huge Archid forms. They also fought other creatures with crazy huge forms and crazy huge sharks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768162#post768162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... also they lose continuity with the Mokole if they don't have any crocodile or turtle forms. How did they survive for long enough to give them the time to change every one of them to breeding with new species of reptiles?</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't need time. The change in animal breeds was Gaia practically wiping the slate clean and starting again millions of years later with smaller creatures. Ananasi and Rokea endured through the ages (Rokea bred themselves into downsizing as years turned ever onwards). Gaia tinkered with the basic design of the surviving shapeshifters, adding additional forms, and opening up the potential for them to have a common breeding partner in the Drachid-like creatures she envisioned in her dreams. She also elevated a whole new slew of shapeshifters, all of which were smaller than the Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> And then she had the fallen Dragon Kings, which she had cursed to ever remember what their folly had wrought. They no longer had dinosaurs to breed with, so she changed them as they slept. They had new forms (and had lost some old ones), and bred with new creatures, but they endured, and the memory endured with them. After all, a curse to remember for all time isn't very curse-y if the cursed ones just sleep through it and then die off. The Mother's anger wasn't going to subside in a few dozen million years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768162#post768162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing... I hope the Drachid are portrayed as therapod dinosaurs with tails and horizontal posture, not human-shaped. Dinosaur skeletons make a human posture physically impossible, and I think reptoids look... silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be flippant, but spider exoskeletons, shark skeletons etc make human posture physically impossible. That's why they're shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry you find reptoids silly. I don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 11-18-2015, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T00:02:55-08:00","id":768321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768190#post768190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Erinys in regard to the animal breed forms. Adding the plesiosaurs and what not was very cool, but I think relying on their breeding rites to gain not just the homid form in place of Drachid but also new verna to replace extinct ones feels like too much of a deux ex machina.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's intended to be deus, as Gaia specifically rewrites the templates of her early shapeshifter experiments, adding forms, shrinking things down to be more consistent with available animals, making new shapeshifters to fill in the gaps, opening a breeding slot that will one day be filled with the hairless tool-users she dreams about, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T00:05:11-08:00","id":768322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768303#post768303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mokole don't have a near human form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to Weekly World News.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T01:11:26-08:00","id":768342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768322#post768322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tell that to Weekly World News.....</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T03:47:33-08:00","id":768400,"title":"","content":"This may not mean much and I'm just adding a few things, please understand that I love 99% of the War of Kings. If you still want to stick with what is written that won't change my order or anything drasitc like that. Just making the disclaimer that this is just a reptile enthusiast typing and not a fanboy warpath:<br /> <br /> oldest Pterasaur species was the Eudimorphodon: about 210 million years ago<br /> oldest dinosaur species was Eoraptor: about 228 million years ago<br /> oldest plesiosaur species was Nichollsia borealis<span style=\"font-size:11px\">: <span style=\"font-size:12px\">112 million years ago</span></span><br /> oldest turtle (with a full carapace and plastron) was the Proganochelys: about 210 million years ago<br /> oldest crocodilian species were Erpetosuchus or Doswellia: about 200 million years ago (also crocodillians got to some fairly impressive sizes like sarcosuchus who got to almost 40 feet, making crocodilians able to grow to sizes on par with carnivorous dinosaurs).<br /> <br /> Also Reptiod form is listed on page 148 of the CB20 as a rank 2 generic gift. Its why I would love to see art for both the Reptoid Form and the Kings to see if my Mokole players can maquarade as something they are not in this setting.<br /> <br /> Again not being an angry fanboy, and if you want things to stick that's how they are. I just wanted to point out that the other kin species for the Kings really aren't older then the animals the Mokole do link themselves to. So maybe its really less about size and age then it is about &quot;not mokole&quot;, though wouldn't that make Mokole rather young as shifters then since they wouldn't have actually arisen until after the mammel shifters like the write up says?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T10:06:10-08:00","id":768573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768303#post768303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mokole don't have a near human form.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 Changing Breeds says otherwise. It's blatantly there as a Rank 2 General Mokole Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T11:27:05-08:00","id":768620,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to echo CeltSPZ I like most of what I read, but the crocodilians are just as old as dinosaurs, and got large at an earlier time. I <i><b>like</b></i> the idea of including dinosaurs and pterosaurs, please don't get me wrong. I understand not including turtles. I'm excited about this regardless, and my concern about the saurid varnas is relatively minor. But crocodyliformes, pseudosuchians, and sea crocodiles were big and really cool back then too. (Plesiosaurs with their small heads don't impress me as much as pliosaurs and sea-crocodiles).<br /> <br /> Mesozoic crocodylomorphs evolved in the Triassic, rapidly got rather large, and some even ate medium-sized dinosaurs. They included fully terrestrial ziphodont forms (with tyrannosaur-like teeth and relatively long legs for running fast) and fully-marine forms of pliosaur size, in addition to amphibious forms resembling to modern crocodilians. If you cast the net a little wider (and why not when dinosaurs and pterosaurs are included) to look at other crurotarsans, there were rauisuchids, postosuchids, phytosaurs, ornithosuchids, and poposuchids of large size (some as large as modern crocodiles, and larger than contemporary dinosaurs and pterosaurs) in the Triassic, such as the 7-meter-long <i>Karamuru</i> (from the mid-Triassic, while the 3-6 m <i>Herrerasaurus</i> didn't evolve until the late Triassic, contemporary with 6-9 m <i>Saurosuchus</i> and the possibly 8-10 m <i>Fasolasuchus</i>). Some of these things were <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Postosuchus\" target=\"_blank\">bipedal</a> and resembled therapod dinosaurs, with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prestosuchus\" target=\"_blank\">jaws and teeth like carnosaurs</a>.<br /> <br /> Triassic true crocodylomorphs were small, but so were most Triassic dinosaurs. (I had always thought the Kings didn't appear until the early Jurassic.) The exceptions I know of were <i>Herrerasaurus</i> and some prosauropods, but they lived alongside the equally large pseudosuchians. Large therapods didn't get top-predator niches until the Triassic extinctions wiped out the crurotarsan competition.<br /> <br /> Fully-shelled turtles evolved in late Triassic, and they also grew to quite large sizes like <i>Archelon</i> during the Mesozoic. Though to be fair CeltSPZ, the horned turtle and giant sea-turtle fossils only go back to the Cretaceous.<br /> <br /> AFAIK Pterosaurs were all quite small and lightweight (up to turkey-weight in the Cretaceous, despite their wingspans) until the Cretaceous Neoazhdarchians evolved: more &quot;puny&quot; than 5-10 m crocodiles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the &quot;reptoids&quot;... please at least give them <b>tails</b>, for the love of Gaia. I beg. <i><b>Please</b></i>. I absolutely cannot stand reptoid 'aliens' from bad scif, they don't in any way resemble dinosaurs. And the mortal Drachids were explicitly not shapeshifters, so making them mammal-dinosaur hybrids... please just don't. Please. The Dinosaur Kings are so awesome because they're a <i><b>dinosaur</b></i> civilization, not for being lizard aliens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have presently forgotten what I knew about Mesozoic sharks. My guess is that, although smaller sharks were available, Rokea weren't interested in them. Since they can breed with any shark &quot;varnas&quot; without any need for a rite, they have less reason to follow specific evolutionary lineages. That said, I don't know of larger-than-modern sharks from in Mesozoic... <i>Megalodon</i> were post-Mesozoic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-18-2015, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T12:48:27-08:00","id":768674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768620#post768620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fully-shelled turtles evolved in late Triassic, and they also grew to quite large sizes like <i>Archelon</i> during the Mesozoic. Though to be fair CeltSPZ, the horned turtle and giant sea-turtle fossils only go back to the Cretaceous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to clear up, the image that I posted was of proganochelys, the oldest known turtle with a carapace and plasteron. From what I've seen they grew comparable to a lot of the earlier pterasours. (Have to defend the turtles)<br /> <br /> On another note, I don't mind reptoids.....I also don't mind the idea that they woke up changed to homid and modern varna. If it was stated in the write up I'm cool with it, if not could it be? I imagined a lone theropod waking up and then using breeding rites for 2 forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-18-2015, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T13:20:34-08:00","id":768694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768674#post768674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I don't mind reptoids.....I also don't mind the idea that they woke up changed to homid and modern varna. If it was stated in the write up I'm cool with it, if not could it be? I imagined a loan theropod waking up and then using breeding rites for 2 forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll make a note for it to be made explicit in the write-up. I suspect this specific detail may have been victim to word count, but it is easy enough to rectify with just a few dozen words. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T13:48:20-08:00","id":768707,"title":"","content":"Given a &quot;Gaia did it&quot; explanation I can imagine a completely different set of saurid varnas being used to emphasize the fallen nature of the Mokole... but I hope that if the authors don't add any crocodyliformes or other crurotarsan predators, that the final chapter at least has a clearer explanation of how they got new Cenozoic varnas, and why Gaia skipped over the largest predators of the Triassic. (Like not making Dragons until the Jurassic, or making them in the Triassic but already predicting the Triassic extinction and planning to make giant dinosaurs and plio-plesiosaurs take over the Earth afterwards.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768674#post768674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanted to clear up, the image that I posted was of proganochelys, the oldest known turtle with a carapace and plasteron. From what I've seen they grew comparable to a lot of the earlier pterasours. (Have to defend the turtles)</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks Meiolaniid to me. (checks Wikipedia) Well so did <i>Proganochelys</i>, apparently. Huh.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand... don't be afraid to just make up imaginary extinct reptiles, preferrably explicitly imaginary. The fossil record is far from complete especially for large predators, high-altitude ecosystems, moist forests, and Antarctica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-18-2015, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T14:06:52-08:00","id":768716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768707#post768707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It looks Meiolaniid to me. (checks Wikipedia) Well so did <i>Proganochelys</i>, apparently. Huh.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand... don't be afraid to just make up imaginary extinct reptiles, preferrably explicitly imaginary. The fossil record is far from complete especially for large predators, high-altitude ecosystems, moist forests, and Antarctica.</div> </div> </div> </div>Made up varna to fill in the fossil gap could be a great stretch goal (that sadly I don't think we'll ever see)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-18-2015, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T18:37:10-08:00","id":768831,"title":"","content":"So it just occurred to me...Mokole-mbembe...not the stream but the individual. He was said to be the first of the Mokole to be born taking on the homid shape. What's his role now? Is he just the first of the generation born after the Kings? Or is he the first former King to wake up (personally I vote for this one)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:34:23-08:00","id":768994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768707#post768707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given a &amp;quot;Gaia did it&amp;quot; explanation I can imagine a completely different set of saurid varnas being used to emphasize the fallen nature of the Mokole... but I hope that if the authors don't add any crocodyliformes or other crurotarsan predators, that the final chapter at least has a clearer explanation of how they got new Cenozoic varnas, and why Gaia skipped over the largest predators of the Triassic. (Like not making Dragons until the Jurassic, or making them in the Triassic but already predicting the Triassic extinction and planning to make giant dinosaurs and plio-plesiosaurs take over the Earth afterwards.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If we ever get to write a complete Age of Dragons book (I'll be pitching one the next time pitch season comes around), we'll have space to delve into reasons and explanations.* We won't be going into this level of detail in the ~7000 words we have available to give the broadest overview of the entire Dragon Wars. <br /> <br /> * Such a hypothetical book would also include More detailed rules on using the Mnesis, crafting Memetics, revised Gifts and Rites etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T00:19:13-08:00","id":769018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=768831#post768831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it just occurred to me...Mokole-mbembe...not the stream but the individual. He was said to be the first of the Mokole to be born taking on the homid shape. What's his role now? Is he just the first of the generation born after the Kings? Or is he the first former King to wake up (personally I vote for this one)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or he's simply a legend. A tale told by primitive people to give meaning to their existence... or shaped by Mnetics to share a laugh.<br /> <br /> Just to throw out some other options. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:44:31-08:00","id":769283,"title":"","content":"Another <b>possible typo</b>: the beginning of the Dragon Wars section appears to say that Gaia created the Ananasi, instead of Queen Ananasa.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Questions: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Are the Dragons' <i><b>insanely gigantic</b></i> archid forms basically Gozilla-sized or what?</li> <li>I'm guessing this won't be addressed in Shattered Dreams, but is the intent here for every single Dragon/Mokole, <i><b>without</b></i> exception, to sleep the entire time from Wonder-Work until after humans evolved? I liked the idea of some of them being awake occasionally during the Age of Sleep (which has its own pretty neat crocodilian varnas), and their arrogant-and-probably-exaggerated claim to have created humanity raises potential and questions about just what they were up to in the Pliocene. Also the wholesale evacuation of Antarctica has more potential than &quot;They all froze in their sleep 'cause Gaia hated them.&quot; (Although &quot;Some Dragons weren't evacuated and are still down there in magic coccoons, the scientists drilling there are in for a surprise&quot; has potential too...)</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, since I've been critical of the few things that actually bugged me in this 1st draft I want to comment also on what I liked.<ul><li>Just having the War of Dragons at all is awesome and making me want to buy this book when it comes out, more than the Wars of Rage material did. I was and remain a big fan of 2nd Ed. Mokole (yes, I know that breedbook has major flaws, but the parts that succeed are <i><b>awesome</b></i> and the Revised/CB20 depiction made me unhappy). Just having some details sketched out about history, politics, and society can makes the Age of Kings much more playable for interested STs (which I probably won't ever find... sigh).</li> <li>And entire Age of Dragons book!? Sweeeeeet.</li> <li>The concept of Mnesis is way cooler and more interesting/unique than what I was imagining in the Age of Kings and really contributes (along with DINOSAURS and not-insane Wyrm) to the sense of a radially different world on a cosmological level.</li> <li>Justification for why metis/innocents didn't exist for hundreds of millions of years.</li> <li>The depiction of the Bunyip here is pretty good. The authors clearly are doing research into the cultures of Australia and coming up with clever solutions for some of the problems in past depictions of these guys, and justification for the Bunyip name, totem, and appearance. They've got their own distinct purpose and projects and explanation of what they were up to and who they did and didn't get along with and everything. (Am I right in interpreting that their uprovoked attack on the Ananasi was because of all their past fights with the Kumo, and just assuming all werespiders were Kumo/hating all werespiders indiscriminately?)</li> <li>The Bunyip tribal weakness doesn't look fun to play at first glance (and I think additional justification is needed for including any animal parts other than from <i>Thylacoleo</i>, <i>Sarcophilus</i>, and Indonesian canids) but the basic concept really helps deal with the &quot;peaceful&quot; depiction, their retreat from the mainland/the dingos, the million-and-one chimeric descriptions of bunyips, etc. It's clever.</li> <li>Australian Corax. Yes they only get one line, but I love that their existence is included at last. And their disappearance, like with the Ao, isn't the same oft-repeated &quot;Some asshole genocidal shapeshifters murderized them all.&quot; Or at least that's only one possibility, along with the much more interesting possibility of an <b><i>entire tribe of Sun-Lost</i></b> who flew off because the Australian Umbra was just too weird and shiny to resist. &quot;Helped&quot; by the Ananasi, of course... I wonder if the Ananasi manipulated them not by open warfare which doesn't seem to be their way, but by sociocultural manipulation to encourage them to abandon their duties and allies and get more obsessed with Dreaming mysteries. It's plausible given the context, and they could still be out there somewhere in some form...</li> </ul><br /> <br /> In my headcanon Australian Corax are named Wahn and Australian Camazotz are named Garkain, but I admit I only did minimal research to find those names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-19-2015, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T12:27:10-08:00","id":769458,"title":"","content":"Glad you liked the Bunyip stuff! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T00:33:27-08:00","id":769801,"title":"","content":"I've been going back through my design notes when I was designing the Age of Dragons, the Mnesis etc., and I've reminded myself why the Dragon Kings are dinosaurs and not crocs, turtles etc. (Besides any debate about when various animals appeared and disappeared.)<br /> <br /> Simply put, when Mokole dream, they dream of being dragons. They have nightmares of their Archid forms that appear in flesh in the first change. These dreams and nightmares (and eventual physical forms) show the Mokole as dinosaurs and great prehistoric creatures. Modern Mokole are bound to modern reptile forms, their Archid legacy reminds them of when they were something more, something wonderful. When they were Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> And they've lost that glory forever, cast out into these smaller, less glorious forms. They survive, but are much reduced in stature.<br /> <br /> If this wasn't true for the Dragon Kings, if they had ancient reptilian varna (regardless of size), it minimises the tragedy of their fall. They can't retain what they lost and still call it lost. They can't dream of former glory if they retain the link to that glory.<br /> <br /> Thematically, that's what I had in mind for something in the World of Darkness, in Werewolf the Apocalypse. The world is doomed, you played a part in that with your poor choices. Welcome to the end.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T00:49:20-08:00","id":769806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=769283#post769283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another <b>possible typo</b>: the beginning of the Dragon Wars section appears to say that Gaia created the Ananasi, instead of Queen Ananasa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a typo. What the modern Ananasi believe and what the ancient Ananasi/Dragon Kings believed don't always have to match. You'll also note the Ananasi history says the Wyld made Gaia and the Weaver made Queen Ananasa, whereas the Werewolf core book says Gaia released the Triat upon the world. <br /> <br /> What's actually true that far back in the pre-times of myth and history is very unclear and prone to being changed depending on who tells the story. The only beings around back then don't tend to speak directly, and the other ancient spirits who reinforce or deny such tales have their own agendas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=769283#post769283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Dragons' <i><b>insanely gigantic</b></i> archid forms basically Gozilla-sized or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many are very big, but not Godzilla sized. Even the biggest dinosaurs were only 18-20 metres tall. Godzilla was around 50m tall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=769283#post769283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing this won't be addressed in Shattered Dreams, but is the intent here for every single Dragon/Mokole, <i><b>without</b></i> exception, to sleep the entire time from Wonder-Work until after humans evolved?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Many didn't sleep. Those who lived more primitively and didn't embrace and abuse the Mnesis, for example. Plus many others who were penitent for their hubris and didn't seek to flee the guilt through sleep.<br /> <br /> They lived on. Many died at the hands of a hostile world (and hostile Ananasi and Rokea). What happened to the rest over millions of years won't be addressed in Shattered Dreams, but opens up possibilities that could one day be explored in a hypothetical Age of Dragons book.<br /> <br /> (Anyone else think a post-apocalyptic Mad Max-type world with the remnants of Dragon civilisation fighting over the last broken, irreplacable Memetic vehicles and devices, while trying to survive marauding Rokea gangs and tribes of Drachid led by Ananasi war-godlings would be cool?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T02:38:32-08:00","id":769832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=769806#post769806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Anyone else think a post-apocalyptic Mad Max-type world with the remnants of Dragon civilisation fighting over the last broken, irreplacable Memetic vehicles and devices, while trying to survive marauding Rokea gangs and tribes of Drachid led by Ananasi war-godlings would be cool?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Me and this is coming from a guy who doesn't really care for the whole war of rage/tears setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T03:33:04-08:00","id":769845,"title":"","content":"I can also get behind this as mad max was how I described it to a friend after I finished reading it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T04:03:27-08:00","id":769854,"title":"","content":"The new Bunyip text is really good. Taking away their solely victim status in the setting, explaining why they didn't breed with dingo.<br /> <br /> AND explaining why no new Bunyip can be born. Very VERY interesting ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T08:14:24-08:00","id":770002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=769806#post769806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many are very big, but not Godzilla sized. Even the biggest dinosaurs were only 18-20 metres tall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing got quite tall like that, but an awful lot got very, very long. Diplodocus has some specimens that are estimated at being 33.5 meters long. Some might be even larger, but are in such terrible fragments that nothing can really be discerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Godzilla was around 50m tall. </div> </div> </div>Original 1954 Godzilla was 50m tall. As buildings got bigger, they started making him bigger in comparison; 2014 Godzilla was nearly 100m tall, and the upcoming Shin Godzilla is slated to be even larger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No. Many didn't sleep. Those who lived more primitively and didn't embrace and abuse the Mnesis, for example. Plus many others who were penitent for their hubris and didn't seek to flee the guilt through sleep.<br /> <br /> They lived on. Many died at the hands of a hostile world (and hostile Ananasi and Rokea). What happened to the rest over millions of years won't be addressed in Shattered Dreams, but opens up possibilities that could one day be explored in a hypothetical Age of Dragons book.<br /> <br /> (Anyone else think a post-apocalyptic Mad Max-type world with the remnants of Dragon civilisation fighting over the last broken, irreplacable Memetic vehicles and devices, while trying to survive marauding Rokea gangs and tribes of Drachid led by Ananasi war-godlings would be cool?) </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8-nhUhw8VV0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted did it.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T13:32:47-08:00","id":770920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=769806#post769806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a typo. What the modern Ananasi believe and what the ancient Ananasi/Dragon Kings believed don't always have to match. You'll also note the Ananasi history says the Wyld made Gaia and the Weaver made Queen Ananasa, whereas the Werewolf core book says Gaia released the Triat upon the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I mistook the writing for being out-of-character God-narrator instead of biased-in-character. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T18:23:27-08:00","id":773558,"title":"","content":"Can't believe I missed this thread until <i>now!</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=769845#post769845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can also get behind this as mad max was how I described it to a friend after I finished reading it!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell you how pumped I am to hear you say that, CeltSPZ. When I was first spit-balling with Bunyip about what I wanted to do with that section of the War of Dragons timeline, my exact words were &quot;prehistoric Mad Max&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T18:50:35-08:00","id":773568,"title":"","content":"For me, a prehistoric mad max was what it felt like reading it and imagining how horrible this had to be for all the Drachids and Kings during/after the fall. I think playing the terror that is the fall and trying to make it when so many are out for your blood could be a blast. Also equally fun I think could be after the Kings awaken, now Mokole. At the very least for my own games, I am going to portray Mokole-mbembe (the individual) as one of the first Kings to awaken in this new fuzzy form, and discover 2 out of 3 forms aren't the same. Have him lead and collect the Kings as they awaken to start to establish this new world they find themselves creating the basis for the Mokole culture we have today. I know Nikink said it's possible he was just a myth, but I want him to have been real due to:<br /> <br /> A) the real world cryptid that he is named after and the Mokole were (at least partially) inspired by<br /> B) the 2 fetishes in the breed book attributed to him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-24-2015, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T16:32:39-08:00","id":775089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/708273-shattered-dreams-2-days-to-go?p=773568#post773568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, a prehistoric mad max was what it felt like reading it and imagining how horrible this had to be for all the Drachids and Kings during/after the fall. I think playing the terror that is the fall and trying to make it when so many are out for your blood could be a blast. Also equally fun I think could be after the Kings awaken, now Mokole. At the very least for my own games, I am going to portray Mokole-mbembe (the individual) as one of the first Kings to awaken in this new fuzzy form, and discover 2 out of 3 forms aren't the same. Have him lead and collect the Kings as they awaken to start to establish this new world they find themselves creating the basis for the Mokole culture we have today. I know Nikink said it's possible he was just a myth, but I want him to have been real due to:<br /> <br /> A) the real world cryptid that he is named after and the Mokole were (at least partially) inspired by<br /> B) the 2 fetishes in the breed book attributed to him</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta say, I would play <i>the hell</i> outta that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd have loved to have more room to cover the proto-Mokole's awakenings (<i>totally </i>plural - I figure many Dragons would have awakened during the Age of Sleep) and the slow process of rebuilding or finding their new place in the world. Remember that the Mnesis is written by the victors (as in, the ones that survive long enough to pass their Mnesis on), which opens it up enough for everyone to have all the pseudepigrapha they want - the culture hero Mhole-mbembe's foundling empire, proto-Mokole toying with early hominids (I like that, but I know a lot of others don't), debased &quot;dragon kingdoms&quot; without the Wonder-Work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}